          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think It Over"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.104,
            0.705,
            0.267,
            0.752
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Are atoms the smallest indivisible particles?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.083,
            0.754,
            0.255,
            0.848
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Why do electrons not fall into the nucleus even though they are attracted to protons in it?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.084,
            0.85,
            0.259,
            0.898
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Why did scientists keep modifying atomic models?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.683,
            0.373,
            0.717
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4 "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Grade 8",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Curiosity "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Chapter 7",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.379,
            0.68,
            0.89,
            0.733
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Everything that you see or "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "observe",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", or feel around is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "matter",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". You have learnt that matter consists of tiny par c es ca e a oms. a e a c oser oo a e p c ure ti l ll d t T k l l k t th i t"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.296,
            0.722,
            0.89,
            0.801
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "given above. What do you observe? Do you "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "notice",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " that both living beings, like us, and non-living things, like a house, are ultimately composed of atoms? These atoms are so tiny that they cannot be seen with the naked eye."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.297,
            0.806,
            0.89,
            0.842
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You may be wondering — Is an atom truly the smallest unit of matter, or can it be divided even further?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.296,
            0.844,
            0.89,
            0.913
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Scientists, too, have been exploring whether atoms are divisible. If so, what are their constituents and how are these arranged? Let us "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "examine",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " how the concept of atoms emerged and how it has been evolved since then."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
